  "reason": "RNA multiprofile scvi_n200 avgpool is currently the strongest direction, but image evidence is sparse because only ResNet50 has been tested and it performed poorly. config_014 tests whether a stronger image representation (ImageNet ViT-L) makes the image modality competitive while keeping profile setting and aggregation fixed to the better ResNet baseline (multiprofile avgpool), cleanly isolating the image encoder effect. This is a high-value use of the next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about whether image features are worth pursuing before investing in multimodal fusion, even if it may not have the highest immediate accuracy."
